leds: lgm-sso: do not set BLINK_R in FPID auto-update mode

SSO_CON0_BLINK_R selects between vendor's regular and high-speed
update path. Mainline lgm-sso enables BLINK_R unconditionally for both
FPID and GPTC modes; the vendor driver only sets it for GPTC-HS and
leaves it cleared for FPID. With BLINK_R asserted in FPID mode the
FPID auto-update divider doesn't actually tick, so writes to SSO_CPU
never reach the shift register.

Match the vendor's behaviour for FPID: clear BLINK_R so the FPID
divider in SSO_CON1 actually drives the auto-update.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
--- a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
@@ -531,8 +531,7 @@ static int sso_gpio_freq_set(struct sso_
 		regmap_update_bits(priv->mmap, SSO_CON1, SSO_CON1_US,
 				   FIELD_PREP(SSO_CON1_US, US_SW));
 	} else if (freq_idx < FPID_FREQ_RANK_MAX) {
-		regmap_update_bits(priv->mmap, SSO_CON0, SSO_CON0_BLINK_R,
-				   SSO_CON0_BLINK_R);
+		regmap_update_bits(priv->mmap, SSO_CON0, SSO_CON0_BLINK_R, 0);
 		regmap_update_bits(priv->mmap, SSO_CON1, SSO_CON1_US,
 				   FIELD_PREP(SSO_CON1_US, US_FPID));
 		regmap_update_bits(priv->mmap, SSO_CON1, SSO_CON1_FPID,
